            <ArticleTitle>Frequency of and outcome of acute coronary syndromes in patients with human immunodeficiency virus infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fifty-one patients with human immunodeficiency virus infection and acute coronary syndromes were identified. Nearly all patients (98%) had traditional coronary risk factors. Revascularization procedures were performed safely with low in-hospital mortality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
